cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use FSMP-kMC in your research, please cite the article below; the software itself can be cited with the metadata in this file."
title: "FSMP-kMC: Field-Stabilized Multiphase kinetic Monte Carlo"
abstract: >-
  A kinetic Monte Carlo engine for the atomistic thermodynamics of rigid
  molecular crystals and two-dimensional adsorption layers. A crystal and an
  ideal-gas reservoir coexist in one elongated cell, held there by an imposed
  damping field and external field, which gives the free energy, entropy and
  chemical potential of the dense layer from the equality of the chemical
  potentials in the coexisting phases. Molecules are rigid bodies with
  continuous positions and orientations, interacting through a precalculated
  numerical pair potential. Ships with FSMP-kMC Studio, a desktop workbench
  covering the whole workflow.
